From: WG2600HP isolated data-path review 2026-11-01
Subject: [CANDIDATE 760-10] qca-8021q: route CPU TX on bridge VID regardless of offload mark

NEVER APPLY to the build or production tree without DSA/ECM/NSS
cross-path, compile, RAM boot and LAN/WAN forwarding verification.
The DSA 802.1Q user-facing VLAN interface is NOT introduced.
Depends on 760-01 qca-8021q tagger and its 760-02/03 switch integration.

dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_join() replaces a user's standalone VID
with its bridge VID. The staged qca_8021q_xmit() used bridge VID
only if skb->offload_fwd_mark was set, so CPU-routed IPv4 output
would still use the deleted standalone VID and risk dropping.
Align bridge VID selection with staged ECM 760-04 for VLAN-unaware
bridges. Handle br==NULL explicitly for offload_fwd_mark.

--- a/net/dsa/tag_qca_8021q.c
+++ b/net/dsa/tag_qca_8021q.c
@@ -65,18 +65,24 @@
 	u16 tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_standalone_vid(dp);
 	u8 pcp;
 
-	if (skb->offload_fwd_mark) {
-		unsigned int bridge_num = dsa_port_bridge_num_get(dp);
-		struct net_device *br = dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp);
-
-		/* A VLAN-aware bridge carries its own VID; the switch
-		 * forwards on that one.
-		 */
-		if (br_vlan_enabled(br))
-			return skb;
-
-		tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(bridge_num);
-	}
+	struct net_device *br = dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp);
+
+	/*
+	 * An offloaded frame in a VLAN-aware bridge already carries the
+	 * bridge VLAN. Do not add a tag_8021q VLAN on top.
+	 */
+	if (skb->offload_fwd_mark && br && br_vlan_enabled(br))
+		return skb;
+
+	/*
+	 * dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_join() replaces the standalone VID with
+	 * a bridge VID. Routed IPv4 output has no offload_fwd_mark, but
+	 * must use the same bridge VID or the switch will drop the frame.
+	 * Match ecm_interface_dsa_8021q_conduit's VID selection.
+	 */
+	if (br && dp->bridge && dp->bridge->tx_fwd_offload &&
+	    !br_vlan_enabled(br))
+		tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(dsa_port_bridge_num_get(dp));
 
